# License API — example environment (E006). Copy the ideas here into your orchestrator's env and
# mount secrets as files. NEVER commit real secrets. See docs/config-reference.md for the full contract.
#
# --- Non-secret runtime settings (safe as plain env) ---
NODE_ENV=production
HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=8080
DB_POOL_MAX=10
SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
LOG_LEVEL=info
#
# --- Secrets: prefer the <VAR>_FILE convention (mounted files), NOT plain env ---
# The API resolves <VAR>_FILE first (file contents, trailing newline trimmed), then falls back to <VAR>.
# DATABASE_URL_FILE=/run/secrets/database_url
# API_KEY_SECRET_FILE=/run/secrets/api_key_secret
# SIGNING_CUSTODIAN_SHARES_FILE=/run/secrets/signing_custodian_shares
#
# Direct (non-file) forms — acceptable for local dev only, discouraged in production:
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://licensesrv:CHANGE_ME@db:5432/licensesrv
# API_KEY_SECRET=CHANGE_ME
#
# --- docker-compose secret files (create these before `docker compose up`) ---
# ./secrets/db_password              -> the Postgres password (e.g. a long random string)
# ./secrets/database_url             -> postgres://licensesrv:<db_password>@db:5432/licensesrv
# ./secrets/api_key_secret           -> the HMAC secret for API-key + email hashing
